<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mikhail Gorbachev</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1931">1931</a>–<a href="/years/2022">2022</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mikhail Gorbachev (1931–2022) was the last leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>, general secretary of the Communist Party from 1985 and president from 1990 to 1991. His policies of glasnost, or openness, and perestroika, or restructuring, loosened censorship and central control, while abroad he ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cold-war">Cold War</a> and allowed the fall of the communist regimes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-europe">Eastern Europe</a> in 1989. He received the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nobel-peace-prize">Nobel Peace Prize</a> in 1990.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mikhail-gorbachev.jpg" alt="Mikhail Gorbachev" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vladimir Vyatkin / Владимир Вяткин; derivative work by Jbarta · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:RIAN_archive_850809_General_Secretary_of_the_CPSU_CC_M._Gorbachev_(crop).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
